      "description": "Watch St. Truiden vs RAAL La Louvière highlights and goals from Jupiler Pro League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 7, 2026. The stage was set for a compelling Jupiler Pro League encounter on September 07, 2026, as St. Truiden hosted Lommel United . Both sides entered the match with high stakes, looking to climb the table and assert their dominance in a high-intensity footballing display. Early Discipline and Tactical Battles The opening stages were characterized by a fierce battle for possession, with neither side willing to give an inch. This physicality led to early intervention from the referee, who handed out yellow cards to Mustapha Isah in the 9th minute and Ilias Sebaoui shortly after in the 13th. The match remained a tight affair for much of the first half, as both defenses held firm against tentative attacking forays. Breaking the Deadlock Before the Interval As the half-time whistle approached, the momentum shifted decisively in favor of the hosts. In the 41st minute, Kaito Matsuzawa provided a sublime assist for Ryan Merlen , who clinical finish broke the deadlock. The goal injected fresh energy into the stadium, giving St. Truiden a vital lead to take into the locker rooms after a hard-fought opening 45 minutes. Second Half Surge and Bazdar's Brace St. Truiden wasted no time doubling their advantage after the restart. In the 54th minute, Ryan Merlen turned provider, setting up Robert-Jan Vanwesemael for a well-taken goal. Despite a series of tactical substitutions from both managers, including the introduction of Wolke Janssens for the hosts, Lommel United struggled to regain their footing, further hampered by a yellow card for Shaquil Delos in the 61st minute. The final twenty minutes belonged to Samed Bazdar . The forward effectively ended any hopes of a comeback with two goals in quick succession. In the 73rd minute, he converted an assist from Abdoulaye Sissako , and just five minutes later, the pair combined again to make it four. By the time the final whistle blew at 90+3, St. Truiden had secured a dominant victory, fueled by a clinical second-half performance."
